{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43698 - PROTEIN:5832",
  "verbalization": "Fluoranthene is implicated in the biological pathway leading to HuT78 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Fluoranthene acts as a target for Ataxin-2, which in turn is targeted by other compounds, including Ajugaciliatin E and (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide. These compounds all ultimately target HuT78, indicating a shared mechanism of action involving Ataxin-2. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Fluoranthene in modulating the activity of Ataxin-2, which may influence HuT78 through a complex network of molecular interactions. The evidence supports a link between Fluoranthene and HuT78 via Ataxin-2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
